Comments get cleaned up recursively through the same DeleteMemo call. Now I want to check whether reactions are handled anywhere in this flow, since I don't see them mentioned yet.

Scanning the API handler again - ListReactions is called but there's no matching Store.DeleteReaction anywhere. Attachments do get deleted via ListAttachments + DeleteAttachment, and comment memos get resolved through ListMemoRelations + recursive DeleteMemo.

So the tables directly touched are: memo, memo_relation (both MemoID and RelatedMemoID sides), and attachment. Reactions seem to be listed but never explicitly removed.

I don't see memo_share handled either. Let me trace through the API handler's full sequence once more: first it deletes comment memos, then calls the store-level DeleteMemo for the target memo itself.

Store.DeleteMemo does three things explicitly: removes memo_relation rows, removes attachment rows, then deletes the memo record. That gives me three tables: memo, memo_relation, attachment.

I'm still unsure about reactions - there's no explicit DeleteReaction call I've found, so either the DB has a foreign key cascade, or reactions are simply orphaned. Since comments recursively go through the same DeleteMemo path, whatever cascade applies to a normal memo also applies when comments get deleted.

